import LeanFM.Session.Syntax

/-- One period of the audio output: the hard deadline behind "No missed audio deadline" and
    "Every block is on time" (spec/Requirements.lean). The output device releases block k at
    t0 + k * P, P = frames / rate (64 / 48000 s = 1333.3 us), whether or not the audio is ready:
    the device is the clock, and the audio cannot make it wait. The audio renders the block and
    hands it over; the device then plays it, if it arrived before release + P, or skips it (an
    underrun: the listener hears a gap). Each block is its own session (its index is the session
    id), so a stream of blocks is a stream of independent trials and a single Skipped anywhere is
    a counterexample. "Eventually Block" is not the requirement: a block that arrives after its
    period is Skipped however soon after it arrives.

    Timestamps (ts, nanoseconds of one monotonic clock): Pull is the release, Block the moment
    the rendered block was handed over, Played or Skipped one nanosecond after Block. The device's
    verdict is exactly: Played iff Block.ts - Pull.ts <= P (in integers, (Block.ts - Pull.ts) *
    rate <= frames * 10^9). The bench (--bench ... --period-log <path>) writes this stream after
    the run from preallocated arrays, never from the audio thread. -/
protocol AudioPeriod (Device, Audio) {
  p: Pull from Device to Audio;
  b: Block from Audio to Device cause p;
  choice {
    Played from Device to Audio cause b;
  } or {
    Skipped from Device to Audio cause b;
  }
}

/- The requirements over one audio period that convert to CTL, each decided by LeanFM
   (session_ctl), none vacuous. Whether a block is Played or Skipped is decided by a deadline
   (Block.ts - Pull.ts <= P), which is not CTL yet, so the two timing requirements are sorry: the
   protocol only says a block may be skipped. -/
requirements {
  "One audio period follows AudioPeriod" => AudioPeriod;
  "A block is rendered only after its release" => AudioPeriod ⊨ (precedes (on Pull) (on Block));
  "Every released block is handed over" => AudioPeriod ⊨ (stronglyImplies (on Pull) (inevitably (on Block)));
  "The device judges a block only after it is handed over" => AudioPeriod ⊨ (precedes (on Block) (or (on Played) (on Skipped)));
  "Every handed-over block is played or skipped" => AudioPeriod ⊨ (stronglyImplies (on Block) (inevitably (or (on Played) (on Skipped))));
  "A played block is never also skipped" => AudioPeriod ⊨ (stronglyImplies (on Played) (never (on Skipped)));
  "Possibly a block is skipped: the device does not wait" => AudioPeriod ⊨ (possibly (on Skipped));
  -- a deadline: every Pull reaches Played, Block within one period P of its Pull
  "Every block is on time" => sorry;
  -- a deadline: never Skipped while NAM, the sympathetic strings and the reverb all run
  "No missed audio deadline" => sorry;
}
